    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0154" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1193</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spencer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-03T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1918,
                                noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 12.16
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Palmer<anchor n="1" xml:id="d94-f1"/> in Irkutsk telegraphs as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>On account of anarchy regulations all commercial transactions are
                            impossible. War prisoners are armed and organized. Maximalists are
                            showing great discontent at Chinese embargo. They fear intervention by
                            Japan or the Allies but such intervention is desired by almost the
                            entire population and appears to be very urgent. Maximalists have warned
                            consuls and foreigners that the country will make reprisals in case of
                            need.</p></quote></p>
                <p>I have transmitted the above to Admiral Knight in Vladivostok and instructed
                    Consul Moser in Harbin to give the Admiral all possible information from every
                    point of view.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spencer</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d94-f1" n="1" xml:id="d94-f1-content">
                <p>William Morgan Palmer, Vice Consul.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
